barbarousness:
中：n. barbarous的变形
英：n. The quality or state of being barbarous; barbarity;
   barbarism.

barefacedness:
中：n. 不戴面具, 不要脸, 无耻, 露骨
英：n. The quality of being barefaced; shamelessness;
   assurance; audaciousness.

basylous:
中：[医] 硷性的, 硷式的
英：a. Pertaining to, or having the nature of, a basyle;
   electro-positive; basic; -- opposed to chlorous.

becomingness:
中：n. becoming的变形
英：n. The quality of being becoming, appropriate, or fit;
   congruity; fitness.

bigly:
中：adv. big的变形
英：a. In a tumid, swelling, blustering manner; haughtily;
   violently.

bird-witted:
中：a. 轻浮的, 心思不专一的
英：a. Flighty; passing rapidly from one subject to another;
   not having the faculty of attention.

bivalved:
中：双瓣的,双壳的
英：a. Having two valves, as the oyster and some seed pods;
   bivalve.

blemishment:
中：n. 瑕疵；污点；缺点 (blemish的变形)
英：n. The state of being blemished; blemish; disgrace;
   damage; impairment.

bond service:
中：奴役
英：The condition of a bond servant; service without wages;
   slavery.

bottone:
中：n. (Bottone)人名；(意)博托内
英：a. Having a bud or button, or a kind of trefoil, at the end;
   furnished with knobs or buttons.

bouget:
中：n. (Bouget)人名；(法)布热
英：n. A charge representing a leather vessel for carrying water;
   -- also called water bouget.

brininess:
中：n. briny的变形
英：n. The state or quality of being briny; saltness;
   brinishness.

buxom:
音标：/'bʌksәm/
中：a. (妇女)丰满的, 健美的
英：s. (of a female body) healthily plump and vigorous;
